{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner answers the five questions of scope contract revision 21 (b68ce5e3, builder's request 22fc1a93, invitation f198dfb8). None blocks the review. (a) The authority note's section 6.5 changes in the three places, as the note decides: every entry the reserve message names gets a written fact type, the count is made at the delivery of reserve, and entries of jobs that are not required are fetched and retained anyway. Sizing every outcome entry for the largest fetch would charge every outcome for one case; counting at reserve is bounded and checkable. (b) Worst-case counting of the states a rule may set is accepted now. A mark naming them is an optimization for later, when the proof plan shows the worst case costs something. (c) Yes, a kind may state that only its first outcome opens children, as a declared and validated property of the kind, never inferred; the default stays the full reservation. (d) Yes, intended: a withdraw of a final publication settles nothing, so it is new work and may wait for room. Answer 3 of 1f8aba72 is about a member's own pending request. (e) Yes, the split is right: the authority note owns what the destination reads, records and reports for the fault state; the lane forms own what a member sees of it."}